  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Justice obligated $8B in federal contract dollars in FY2026 to date. The Department of Justice made 44,927 awards with an average award size of $178K. Obligations are down 6.7% year over year. Fiscal totals are partial because FY2026 is a fiscal year to date reporting period, but the multi-year series shows obligations were $9.1B in FY21, $9B in FY22, $10B in FY23, $9.4B in FY24, and $8.5B in FY25. Other Computer Related Services is the largest NAICS category in FY2026 to date at $944M, followed by Security Guards and Patrol Services at $771M and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $706M. METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is the top vendor in FY2026 to date at $524M, followed by NAPHCARE LLC at $207M and MCKESSON CORPORATION at $172M. This snapshot highlights where current contract dollars concentrate by industry and by supplier within the Department of Justice procurement portfolio.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How large are Justice's FY2026 contract obligations compared with prior years?",
        "body": "The Department of Justice obligated $8B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Justice obligated $9.1B in FY21, $9B in FY22, $10B in FY23, $9.4B in FY24, and $8.5B in FY25. Obligations are down 6.7% year over year. The Department of Justice made 44,927 awards so far, with an average award size of $178K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Justice's biggest purchase categories and who gets the money?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the largest NAICS category at $944M in FY2026 to date, followed by Security Guards and Patrol Services at $771M and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals at $706M. METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is the largest vendor at $524M, followed by NAPHCARE LLC at $207M and MCKESSON CORPORATION at $172M. The top ten categories and top ten vendors together show a mix of IT, security, medical, and support services concentrating the Department of Justice contract dollars."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Justice spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Justice obligated $8B in FY2026 to date. The Department of Justice recorded 44,927 awards with an average award size of $178K. Obligations are down 6.7% year over year and prior fiscal-year totals were $9.1B in FY21, $9B in FY22, $10B in FY23, $9.4B in FY24, and $8.5B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Justice buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Justice buys a mix of IT, security, medical, and facility support services. Other Computer Related Services is $944M, Security Guards and Patrol Services is $771M, General Medical and Surgical Hospitals is $706M, and other major categories include Computer Systems Design Services at $465M and All Other Legal Services at $370M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Justice's largest contractors?",
      "a": "METROPOLITAN SECURITY SERVICES, INC. is the largest contractor at $524M. Other top contractors include NAPHCARE LLC at $207M, MCKESSON CORPORATION at $172M, AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC at $154M, and CGI FEDERAL INC. at $149M."
